'''Yarkora''',<ref name="beware">''[[Return of the Jedi: Beware the Power of the Dark Side!]]''</ref> also known as '''Yarkorans''' and '''Yak Faces''', were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] found in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="A Friend in Need Episode Guide" /> [[Saelt-Marae]]<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> and [[Jedi Master]] [[Adampo]]<ref name="Into the Dark">''[[The High Republic: Into the Dark]]''</ref> were Yarkorans.<ref name="A Friend in Need Episode Guide" /> Due to most Yarkora eating constantly throughout the [[Standard day|day]], they had two [[stomach]]s, four [[kidney]]s, and three [[liver]]s.<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know" />

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
In the very first draft of the script for "[[A Friend in Need]]," the fourteenth episode of the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' television series']] [[The Clone Wars: Season Four|fourth season]], the planet [[Carlac]] was to be inhabited by Yarkora&mdash;although the name was spelled "Yakoran" on some pieces of concept art. Ultimately, however, the inhabitants of Carlac were turned into the "much more sympathetic and relatable" [[Ming Po]] people.<ref name="FIN Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/a-friend-in-need-trivia-gallery|text="A Friend in Need" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 2}}</ref>

